  concept: 'Authored objective: Commission four cameras, LiDAR and IMU.

    Authored
    requirement: Measure trigger skew, calibrate both stereo pairs, the LiDAR range
    and IMU bias.

    General teaching principle: Sensor outputs require proper
    calibration, reference and freshness before they can support a diagnosis.

    Only
    fresh, authoritative game evidence can establish that this objective is complete.'
  analogy: A measuring ruler is useful only if zero and units are correctly established.
  diagram: '[Authored setup] -> [Check prerequisites] -> [Observe the game evidence]
    -> [Verify objective]'
  misconception: An old, uncalibrated or missing sensor reading is not reliable evidence.
